            <ArticleTitle>Retroperitoneal Cyst: An Uncommon Presentation of Filariasis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>674252</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2015/674252</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary retroperitoneal parasitic cysts are rare. Here we report about a middle aged male patient from rural north India with a recent onset of central abdominal retroperitoneal lump, pain, and fever. After surgical resection due to diagnostic uncertainty, at histopathology, it turned out be a filarial cyst. After receiving a course of diethylcarbamazine, the patient is asymptomatic at 4 months' follow-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
